spans.s:
3sa, one, in sa-kṛt, sa-hasra. [for *sm
(vocalic m), root *sem: cf. εἷς, *σεμ-ς,
μία, *σμ-ια, ‘one’; ἑ-κατόν, ‘one-hundred’;
ἁ-πλόος, ‘one-fold’; Lat. sem-el, ‘once’;
sim-plex, ‘one-fold’; ἄ-λοχος, ‘having one
(i. e. one and the same) bed, spouse’;
ὄ-πατρος, ‘having one (i. e. one and the
same) father’; ἀ-δελφός, see under garbha.
]
